# Error handling

Curated from TS/JS code-quality rule packs; use dammo patterns.

## Server

```typescript
// ✅ Throw AppError; createApp() maps isAppError → { error, code }
throw new AppError('Not found', 404, 'NOT_FOUND');

// ❌ Empty catch or swallowing errors
try { await work(); } catch {}
```

- Prefer `AppError` from `server/src/shared/http/errors.ts` for expected failures.
- Log unexpected errors server-side; do not leak stacks to JSON responses.

## Client

```typescript
if (isAbortError(err)) return;
setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : t('…fallbackKey'));
```

- Use `isAbortError` from `client/src/api/http.ts` when requests pass `signal`.
- User-facing fallbacks go through i18n (`t(...)`), not hardcoded strings.
